        "title": "Ray Tracing",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The naming convention is \"backward\" ray tracing — rays travel *from* the eye *into* the\nscene, the reverse of physical photons, because we only care about the light that actually\nreaches the camera. The whole field is built on one geometric primitive (ray-surface\nintersection) and one organizing principle (recursion)."
    },
